id: pm-ay3l0p
title: Nested pm test coverage changes repository-root fixtures because outer PM_PATH sandboxing leaks into package-owned run-tests
description: "Running node scripts/run-tests.mjs coverage directly from the checkout passes all 381 files and 6,451 tests at 100/100/100/100. Linking the identical command through pm test fails 11 validate ownership/path-classification cases under schema context and the same cases plus merge-receipt context under tracker context. The outer linked-test runner replaces PM_PATH with a temporary schema or tracker copy; repository-root validation fixtures then derive ownership and path candidates from the copied tracker rather than the checkout, despite run-tests.mjs providing its own inner test sandboxes. This makes the documented package-owned sandbox runner unsafe to compose as a broad linked test and produces false product failures."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: "area:cli","area:testing",context-integrity,developer-experience,sandbox
created_at: "2026-07-28T14:04:06.683Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-07T09:25:17.031Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-07T09:24:56.962Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-07T09:24:56.962Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Direct and pm-linked executions of node scripts/run-tests.mjs coverage produce the same test and coverage result; No unit or integration test reads or writes the real repository .agents/pm tracker; Schema and tracker linked-test modes retain their documented semantics for genuine pm commands
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make package-owned test runners compositionally isolated when invoked through pm linked-test sandboxes
value: The same authoritative coverage command should have one result whether run directly or through PM evidence orchestration
impact: Prevents false coverage failures and lets broad gates be recorded as executable PM evidence without exposing the real tracker
outcome: "run-tests.mjs derives repository fixtures from the checkout while every test PM read/write remains sandboxed, and a nested pm test regression proves parity"
why_now: PR #795 exact-head verification produced repeatable direct-green/linked-red evidence in both schema and tracker modes
parent: pm-92if
risk: high
confidence: 85
severity: medium
resolution: Cleared inherited PM_SOURCE_PM_PATH and PM_SOURCE_WORKSPACE_ROOT at the inner run-tests sandbox boundary while preserving isolated PM_PATH and PM_GLOBAL_PATH roots.
expected_result: Package-owned coverage remains 100/100/100/100 under a linked PM run without repository-root fixture drift
actual_result: "Direct and pm-linked full coverage now both pass 441 files and 6,919 tests at exact 100/100/100/100; the source checkout tracker remains outside the test PM roots."
component: linked test sandbox composition
regression: false
