comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-28T14:04:06.683Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: searched all statuses for linked-test coverage outer PM_PATH repository ownership fixtures and run-tests coverage tracker isolation. Results covered general coverage and CI lineage but no item owned this reproducible nested-sandbox parity gap."
  "2026-08-04T19:54:05.741Z","harness:codex","Reproduction 2026-08-04: pm test pm-5t33or --run nested the linked node scripts/run-tests.mjs coverage command under the default schema PM_PATH. Direct coverage on the identical checkout passed 433 files and 6,850 tests at 100/100/100/100; nested execution failed 12 validate-command repository ownership/path-classification assertions because it inspected the empty outer schema context. This exactly reproduces the canonical direct-green/linked-red acceptance gap; no duplicate item created."
  "2026-08-07T09:24:56.072Z","harness:codex","Evidence: fixed nested package-owned test isolation by clearing PM_SOURCE_PM_PATH and PM_SOURCE_WORKSPACE_ROOT only after run-tests.mjs establishes fresh PM_PATH and PM_GLOBAL_PATH roots. Regression: focused runner passed 15/15. Canonical pm-linked coverage passed 441 files and 6,919 tests at exact 100/100/100/100 (49,663 statements, 36,088 branches, 10,157 functions, 48,108 lines), followed by the focused linked test passing. This closes the repeated direct-green/linked-red gap without exposing or mutating the real tracker."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-07T09:24:56.470Z","harness:codex","A self-sandboxing child runner must treat outer PM_SOURCE_* variables as authority-bearing context, not harmless metadata. Reset inherited source-location hints at the same boundary that replaces PM_PATH and PM_GLOBAL_PATH, while leaving genuine linked commands' execution context unchanged."
files[2]{path,scope,note}:
  scripts/run-tests.mjs,project,Clears inherited source-workspace hints when creating the authoritative inner test sandbox
  tests/unit/scripts/run-tests.spec.ts,project,Regression proves child test processes cannot inherit outer linked-test source hints
